1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,331
At eleven forty, the apartment finally became quiet. After

2
00:00:04,331 --> 00:00:08,662
a day answering people, nobody needed him. He did

3
00:00:08,662 --> 00:00:12,993
not know what to do with the silence.

4
00:00:13,413 --> 00:00:16,428
He stood at the refrigerator without opening it. He

5
00:00:16,428 --> 00:00:19,443
was not especially hungry. He wanted the day to

6
00:00:19,443 --> 00:00:22,457
feel different without another question.

7
00:00:22,877 --> 00:00:25,751
His phone was already in his hand. There was

8
00:00:25,751 --> 00:00:28,624
a familiar place he went when he wanted to

9
00:00:28,624 --> 00:00:31,498
feel something else. The first few seconds always seemed

10
00:00:31,498 --> 00:00:34,371
to loosen the pressure.

11
00:00:34,791 --> 00:00:37,872
He told himself it would be brief. He was

12
00:00:37,872 --> 00:00:40,952
allowed a break. But the break had no shape.

13
00:00:40,952 --> 00:00:44,033
Another screen was easier than an ending.

14
00:00:44,453 --> 00:00:47,367
Outside, a bus passed the empty stop. Inside, the

15
00:00:47,367 --> 00:00:50,281
light moved across his face while the rest of

16
00:00:50,281 --> 00:00:53,195
the room remained dark. He barely noticed the time

17
00:00:53,195 --> 00:00:56,109
changing.

18
00:00:56,529 --> 00:00:59,466
At one thirty, he put the phone down. Nothing

19
00:00:59,466 --> 00:01:02,404
terrible had happened. Nothing had been repaired, either. The

20
00:01:02,404 --> 00:01:05,341
loneliness he had set aside was waiting beside the

21
00:01:05,341 --> 00:01:08,278
bed.

22
00:01:08,698 --> 00:01:12,086
He promised himself tomorrow would be different. A promise

23
00:01:12,086 --> 00:01:15,473
made after midnight could feel enormous. By morning, it

24
00:01:15,473 --> 00:01:18,860
was mostly exhaustion, with another reason to avoid looking

25
00:01:18,860 --> 00:01:22,247
at himself.

26
00:01:22,667 --> 00:01:25,616
On the table lay an invitation to a Wednesday

27
00:01:25,616 --> 00:01:28,565
drawing group. A neighbor had mentioned it. Three Wednesdays

28
00:01:28,565 --> 00:01:31,514
had passed without him.

29
00:01:31,934 --> 00:01:34,956
That afternoon, he saw the neighbor carrying a sketchbook.

30
00:01:34,956 --> 00:01:37,977
How was the group, he asked. Quiet, she said.

31
00:01:37,977 --> 00:01:40,999
We drew a crooked kettle. You would have fitted

32
00:01:40,999 --> 00:01:44,020
right in.

33
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:47,699
He watched his smile fade in the hallway mirror.

34
00:01:47,699 --> 00:01:50,957
He did not want a flawless life. He wanted

35
00:01:50,957 --> 00:01:54,216
evenings that contained something he could actually remember.

36
00:01:54,636 --> 00:01:59,032
That night, the familiar urge arrived again. He reached

37
00:01:59,032 --> 00:02:03,428
automatically, then noticed the timing. It was strongest after

38
00:02:03,428 --> 00:02:07,825
difficult days, when the apartment first became quiet.

39
00:02:08,245 --> 00:02:12,166
He drew a rough map: a hard day, an

40
00:02:12,166 --> 00:02:16,087
empty room, a quick escape, and the same unmet

41
00:02:16,087 --> 00:02:20,008
need. It described his own evenings. It was not

42
00:02:20,008 --> 00:02:23,930
a diagnosis of everyone else's.

43
00:02:24,350 --> 00:02:27,336
Under the map, he wrote a question. What am

44
00:02:27,336 --> 00:02:30,323
I hoping this will give me tonight? Excitement, sometimes.

45
00:02:30,323 --> 00:02:33,310
Comfort, sometimes. Often it was simply a way not

46
00:02:33,310 --> 00:02:36,296
to feel alone.

47
00:02:36,716 --> 00:02:40,246
The answer did not erase the urge. He still

48
00:02:40,246 --> 00:02:43,775
wanted the easy exit. But he had another choice

49
00:02:43,775 --> 00:02:47,305
besides obeying immediately or insulting himself.

50
00:02:47,725 --> 00:02:50,386
He filled a glass, opened the window, and stayed

51
00:02:50,386 --> 00:02:53,048
there until he had finished drinking. A small pause,

52
00:02:53,048 --> 00:02:55,709
not a miracle. The night air was cold enough

53
00:02:55,709 --> 00:02:58,371
to notice.

54
00:02:58,791 --> 00:03:01,488
He moved the charger out of the bedroom. He

55
00:03:01,488 --> 00:03:04,186
was changing the route his hand knew, without pretending

56
00:03:04,186 --> 00:03:06,883
it had stopped remembering.

57
00:03:07,303 --> 00:03:10,020
Then he took out an old sketchbook. On the

58
00:03:10,020 --> 00:03:12,737
first page, he drew the glass badly. The ellipse

59
00:03:12,737 --> 00:03:15,453
tilted. He left it that way. The glass stayed

60
00:03:15,453 --> 00:03:18,170
on the table.

61
00:03:18,590 --> 00:03:21,249
Twenty minutes later, he wanted the phone again. Drawing

62
00:03:21,249 --> 00:03:23,907
had not replaced every feeling he was avoiding. He

63
00:03:23,907 --> 00:03:26,566
put the pencil down and admitted that he missed

64
00:03:26,566 --> 00:03:29,225
having people around.

65
00:03:29,645 --> 00:03:32,597
He sent one message to a friend he had

66
00:03:32,597 --> 00:03:35,548
stopped answering. Nothing polished. I have been disappearing a

67
00:03:35,548 --> 00:03:38,500
bit. Want to walk this weekend? Then he left

68
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:41,452
the phone face down.

69
00:03:41,872 --> 00:03:45,583
The next evening was worse. A plan fell through.

70
00:03:45,583 --> 00:03:49,295
He came home angry and returned to the familiar

71
00:03:49,295 --> 00:03:53,006
loop before he had even turned on the lamp.

72
00:03:53,426 --> 00:03:57,150
Afterward, the old verdict was ready: you have learned

73
00:03:57,150 --> 00:04:00,874
nothing. He recognized that sentence too. Turning one difficult

74
00:04:00,874 --> 00:04:04,598
evening into his identity had never helped him understand

75
00:04:04,598 --> 00:04:08,322
the evening.

76
00:04:08,742 --> 00:04:12,210
Instead, he added a line to his map. Canceled

77
00:04:12,210 --> 00:04:15,679
plans. Angry. Home alone. The details were useful. The

78
00:04:15,679 --> 00:04:19,147
insult was not. He cleaned the table and left

79
00:04:19,147 --> 00:04:22,616
the sketchbook open.

80
00:04:23,036 --> 00:04:26,818
His second map was smaller: notice the moment, name

81
00:04:26,818 --> 00:04:30,600
the need, choose a response. Sometimes the response was

82
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:34,381
drawing. Sometimes it was rest, a conversation, or asking

83
00:04:34,381 --> 00:04:38,163
someone for help.

84
00:04:38,583 --> 00:04:41,689
His friend answered on Friday. Sunday works. He reread

85
00:04:41,689 --> 00:04:44,795
the message, then caught himself trying to make one

86
00:04:44,795 --> 00:04:47,900
walk carry the weight of his whole future. It

87
00:04:47,900 --> 00:04:51,006
was only a walk.

88
00:04:51,426 --> 00:04:54,482
On Sunday, they walked past closed shops and talked

89
00:04:54,482 --> 00:04:57,539
about ordinary things. He did not deliver a speech

90
00:04:57,539 --> 00:05:00,595
about becoming better. He said the evenings had been

91
00:05:00,595 --> 00:05:03,651
getting away from him.

92
00:05:04,071 --> 00:05:06,869
His friend listened. Then admitted that quiet rooms could

93
00:05:06,869 --> 00:05:09,667
be difficult for him too. Neither one fixed the

94
00:05:09,667 --> 00:05:12,465
other. They made another plan, with an actual day

95
00:05:12,465 --> 00:05:15,263
attached to it.

96
00:05:15,683 --> 00:05:18,441
On Wednesday, he stood outside the drawing room holding

97
00:05:18,441 --> 00:05:21,198
his old sketchbook. Through the window, he could see

98
00:05:21,198 --> 00:05:23,956
the kettle. It was even more crooked than he

99
00:05:23,956 --> 00:05:26,713
had imagined.

100
00:05:27,133 --> 00:05:30,509
He almost left. Arriving meant being seen as a

101
00:05:30,509 --> 00:05:33,884
beginner. He pushed the door anyway. Someone moved a

102
00:05:33,884 --> 00:05:37,260
chair, and he sat down before he could turn

103
00:05:37,260 --> 00:05:40,635
hesitation into another evening.

104
00:05:41,055 --> 00:05:44,387
His drawing was clumsy. Across the table, somebody had

105
00:05:44,387 --> 00:05:47,719
made the kettle look like a shoe. They laughed

106
00:05:47,719 --> 00:05:51,052
about it. Imperfection finally belonged to a room, not

107
00:05:51,052 --> 00:05:54,384
a private verdict.

108
00:05:54,804 --> 00:05:58,176
At eleven forty that night, the apartment became quiet

109
00:05:58,176 --> 00:06:01,549
again. The quiet was still there. So was the

110
00:06:01,549 --> 00:06:04,922
familiar temptation. But the day had contained a conversation

111
00:06:04,922 --> 00:06:08,294
and something made with his hands.

112
00:06:08,714 --> 00:06:11,324
He put the phone on its charger outside the

113
00:06:11,324 --> 00:06:13,933
bedroom. Not as a punishment, and not as proof

114
00:06:13,933 --> 00:06:16,542
that he was cured. It was a boundary he

115
00:06:16,542 --> 00:06:19,152
wanted to keep tonight.

116
00:06:19,572 --> 00:06:22,854
Some evenings still went badly. He began talking honestly

117
00:06:22,854 --> 00:06:26,137
about that, too. If the pattern kept feeling beyond

118
00:06:26,137 --> 00:06:29,420
his control, he could seek support instead of carrying

119
00:06:29,420 --> 00:06:32,703
it as a secret.

120
00:06:33,123 --> 00:06:35,868
He was not trying to become someone who needed

121
00:06:35,868 --> 00:06:38,614
nothing. He was learning to notice what he needed,

122
00:06:38,614 --> 00:06:41,360
and to build an evening that could hold more

123
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:44,106
than a moment of escape.
